  "reasoning": "The patient presents with a high fever and persistent shivering/chills, indicating an acute systemic infection. The presence of rashes on the arms and red patches on the neck points toward a viral exanthem. While malaria commonly causes high fever and chills, it rarely presents with prominent skin rashes. Dengue also features fever and rash but is typically accompanied by severe body pain, headache, and vomiting, which are not mentioned here. The specific combination of high fever, chills, and a rash localized to the arms and neck closely matches the clinical progression of chicken pox, which often begins with constitutional symptoms like fever and malaise before developing into characteristic skin lesions. Based on the symptom profile and matching against known clinical patterns, chicken pox is the most accurate diagnosis.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]chicken pox[/DIAGNOSIS]"
